  "policy_quote": "For a pending order, each item can be modified to an available new item of the same product but of different product option. There cannot be any change of product types, e.g. modify shirt to shoe. The user must provide a payment method to pay or receive refund of the price difference. If the user provides a gift card, it must have enough balance to cover the price difference.",

  "evidence_quote": "→ TOOL_CALL modify_pending_order_items: {\"order_id\": \"#W1845024\", \"item_ids\": [\"1340995114\", \"7493556126\", \"8323284863\"], \"new_item_ids\": [], \"payment_method_id\": \"paypal_3169710\"}",

  "analysis": "The policy explicitly states that items in a pending order can only be modified to **new items of the same product** (e.g., replacing a shirt with another shirt). The current move attempts to **remove items entirely** (by passing an empty `new_item_ids` array), which violates the rule that items must be replaced, not deleted. The evidence confirms this violation: `new_item_ids: []` indicates no replacement items are provided, effectively removing the items rather than modifying them to another option of the same product.",

  "verdict": "SUPPORTED"
}
